Backport of nim-lang/Nim#25858 (fixes #25857) onto the 2.2.10 source tree.

`typeof(result)` inside result's own initializer was counted as a use-before-init
of `result`. The definite-assignment pass `track` (compiler/sempass2.nim) recurses
into every child including `nkTypeOfExpr`, but `typeof(e)` never evaluates `e`, so
calling `useVar` on the inner `result` is wrong. PR #25151 escalated the resulting
spurious ProveInit warning to a hard error, breaking the `ok(typeof(result), v)` /
`?` constructor idiom on {.requiresInit.} result types. Skip nkTypeOfExpr in track.

The track prologue is identical across 2.2.x and devel, so the upstream one-hunk
fix applies unchanged. Merged upstream; drop this patch once a 2.2.x containing
#25858 ships.

--- a/compiler/sempass2.nim
+++ b/compiler/sempass2.nim
@@ -1240,4 +1240,6 @@ proc track(tracked: PEffects, n: PNode) =
 proc track(tracked: PEffects, n: PNode) =
   case n.kind
+  of nkTypeOfExpr:
+    discard "typeof() never evaluates its operand; not a definite-assignment use"
   of nkSym:
     useVar(tracked, n)
